  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Comment cards can identify a room, an object, or a point in the visit.\", \"decision\": \"How should visitor comments be connected to places?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVisitors choose a room on the comment card and then describe the object or moment involved. Comments are first grouped by place.\nThe comment card shows the visit route, and visitors mark where an object or moment stood out. Place and experience are recorded together on a route.\nVisitors describe an object or moment, and volunteers add the relevant room to the comment card. Visitors can express the experience before classifying it."
    }
